1
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:32,640
The End How could this have happened?

2
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,540
I can't believe.

3
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,660
We totally fell for it.

4
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:59,360
Let's go.

5
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:14,757
The men are going to go to the

6
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,037
moon The moon will be on the

7
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:24,397
moon The moon will be on the

8
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:30,800
moon The moon will be on the moon

9
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,900
Having managed to halt the
lovers' invasive attack,

10
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:19,797
Jotaro and company choose to avoid the
political unrest in Iran and Iraq and

11
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:25,240
instead cross the Arabian Sea at Karachi
to arrive at the United Arab Emirates.

12
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:29,117
Now then, if you'd be so kind
as to sign this document,

13
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,620
Everything will be squared away, sir.

14
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:33,110
Hmm.

15
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,460
Right here, yes?

16
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,300
Man, oh, man.

17
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:43,257
You know, I'm the kind of guy who'd
do almost anything for a pretty girl,

18
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,380
even by a car.

19
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,840
My, aren't you sweet?

20
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:49,627
How would you feel about the two
of us having dinner sometime?

21
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:51,660
Sorry, Polnareff.

22
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:56,400
I hate to interrupt when you're
obviously so busy, but... Mr. Joestar!

23
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,447
Come on, it's time to leave.

24
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,077
Seriously, try not to mess with the hair.

25
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:04,137
Do you know how hard it is
to make it look this good?

26
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:06,720
As if anybody cares about your hairdo.

27
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,000
You're driving.

28
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:10,490
Right-o.

29
00:03:10,573 --> 00:03:11,800
Au River, mademoiselle.

30
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:14,320
Hey, Mr. Joestar,

31
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:19,641
I don't get why we're riding in such a fancy
expensive car in this sandy death trap.

32
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:23,505
Wouldn't it be better for us to
get an off-road vehicle instead?

33
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,720
Oh, there's a method to my madness.

34
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:34,140
C 'est magnifique!

35
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:35,873
This country's amazing.

36
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,259
Are you guys seeing what I am here?

37
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:41,537
It's like every house is a
crazy mansion or something.

38
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,450
Yeah.

39
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,220
In Tokyo, a house like one of these
would cost 3 or 4 billion yen.

40
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:51,726
However, for most people in this
country, it's standard living.

41
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:55,780
It wasn't but 20 years ago that
this place was a barren desert,

42
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:58,452
though thanks to a thriving oil industry,

43
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:01,077
it's grown into a playground for the rich.

44
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:04,317
The sun is merciless, but at
least with air conditioning,

45
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,871
it's perfectly comfortable inside the car.

46
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,620
So no complaints here.

47
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,830
Huh?

48
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:12,900
What's wrong, Kakyoin?

49
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,417
It's nothing.

50
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:16,817
I was just thinking about
how open it is here.

51
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:19,440
I know we could spot anyone following us,

52
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:23,957
but I just can't shake the feeling that
there's someone out there watching.

53
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,981
Yeah, can't say that I blame you.

54
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:28,600
Well, back to business.

55
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,817
I've given a bit of thought
to the route we should take.

56
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:35,717
About a hundred kilometers northwest
is a village called Yarplein.

57
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:39,800
The desert and mountains make taking
a direct route near impossible.

58
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,800
It normally takes two
days to reach my car,

59
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:46,817
so to expedite the travel time, the
locals use a Cessna to get there.

60
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,420
If you want my opinion,

61
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,517
we should go to the
village and buy a Cessna

62
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,424
in order to cross the
vast Saudi Arabian desert.

63
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:57,457
You know, I've been apprehensive
about getting anywhere near a plane.

64
00:04:57,540 --> 00:05:00,057
If a stand user attacked
and the plane went down,

65
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:02,297
we'd be putting innocent
lives in harm's way.

66
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:04,757
But if we had a Cessna,
I could be the pilot.

67
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:07,477
We'd be able to save a
couple of days for sure.

68
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:11,057
Flying in a Cessna with a man
who's been in three plane crashes.

69
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,669
Yeah, that seems like
a perfect idea to me.

70
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,140
That comment notwithstanding,

71
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:20,777
our priority should be crossing the desert

72
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:23,197
and hightailing it to
the village of Yarpline.

73
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:25,440
It'll take us one day on Camelback.

74
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,230
Camelback?

75
00:05:27,313 --> 00:05:29,453
A Cessna is one thing, but on Camelback?

76
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,736
I've never ridden a camel in my life!

77
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:35,267
Just leave everything to me.

78
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:38,537
I know these creatures well, and
I'll teach you how to ride them.

79
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:41,580
You boys sit back and
watch the magic happen.

80
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,280
You want camels, you say?

81
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:48,317
Sure I have them, but
they're gonna cost you,

82
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:50,753
my friend, and they need a gentle touch.

83
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:55,577
We're kind of in a life-or-death situation
here, so we need them, whatever it takes.

84
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,425
As for payment, how about
a trade for that car?

85
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:04,000
I couldn't possibly accept such a
generous offer! Yeah, Mr. Joestar!

86
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:07,184
And besides, you literally
just bought that car!

87
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:11,557
What other reason did you think I had
to buy such a fancy, expensive car?

88
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:14,757
It's true an off-road vehicle
would perform better here,

89
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,605
but we're not in the big city.

90
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:19,191
We can't just write a check in this place.

91
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,600
And cash isn't accepted here.

92
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:25,995
In my experience, trading is far more
effective in places such as these.

93
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:29,592
If you try to buy safety for
cheap in a time of emergency,

94
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:32,565
you'll find yourself even
worse off in the end.

95
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:36,917
Besides, I don't know about you, but
I think we've suffered enough already.

96
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,380
Hey, mister! Huh?

97
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:41,160
I take it this seals the deal?

98
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,180
Oh, hey, you know what?

99
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:47,753
To make things a little more even, I'd
like the water in those tanks, too.

100
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:50,837
It's the most important thing
when you're in the desert.

101
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:54,460
But the water isn't nearly
as valuable as your car, sir.

102
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:57,600
You are very strange indeed, sir.

103
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,116
All right, everyone.

104
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,849
Let's get ready, shall we?

105
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,460
Crossing the desert will be no easy task.

106
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,974
Brace yourselves, men.

107
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:12,500
Man, that stinks!

108
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:14,260
Hey, Mr.

109
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,137
Joestar, how the heck are we supposed
to get on one of these things?

110
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:18,867
It's like three meters tall!

111
