Allow me to demonstrate the
proper way to mount a camel.

112
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,059
You have to make them sit
first and then you get on.

113
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,940
Like I said, make them
sit and then get on.

114
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,937
You see, just like this.

115
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:36,900
You make them sit, and
then you get on them.

116
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,700
Give me a minute.

117
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:43,420
Any second this beast is gonna
sit, then let me saddle up.

118
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,360
Hey, sit down, would you?

119
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,140
Damn it, you star! Mr.

120
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:52,077
Joe Star, you have ridden one
of these before, haven't you?

121
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:54,097
I will have you know that
I've watched Lawrence

122
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:56,980
of Arabia three times
now from start to finish.

123
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,960
I know all too well how to ride a camel,

124
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,577
although two of those times
I slept through half of it.

125
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:04,557
You learned to ride from a movie?

126
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:08,580
So you're saying you've never
actually ridden one before?

127
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:19,320
The saliva makes great
sunscreen, the more you know.

128
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:22,580
Listen up.

129
00:08:22,820 --> 00:08:24,517
When you're handling an animal,

130
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:28,247
it's absolutely imperative to
understand exactly how it feels.

131
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,420
And I mean exactly.

132
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:34,531
Here, doesn't this yummy apple
look absolutely scrumptious?

133
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,760
It's really good.

134
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,110
Come on.

135
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,620
Come on.

136
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,140
There's a good boy.

137
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,080
You see?

138
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:43,880
I made the camel sit down.

139
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:48,924
If you just take the time to get inside
its head, it'll sit down for you for sure.

140
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:53,340
Whoa, I did it!

141
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:57,540
Whoa, it's so high off the ground.

142
00:08:57,980 --> 00:08:59,000
By the way,

143
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:04,117
did you know camels can close their
nostrils to keep the sand out and before i

144
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:09,377
forget you're forbidden from making
stupid camel jokes is that understood your

145
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:14,737
turn now you greenhorns get to learn the
finer points of riding a camel listen

146
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:19,157
up the first thing you need to know is
that camels don't walk anything like horses

147
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:22,897
the front and back legs on either side
move forward together so these things

148
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:26,897
can sway a lot but don't let that throw
you off if you find a way to ride with a

149
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:33,117
camel's rhythm i know you'll be just fine
for example yeah hey wait you're going

150
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:39,600
too fast slow down listen to me damn it
yeah i didn't tell you to go that way

151
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:48,620
okay then now that everyone's gotten the
hang of mounting and riding their camels

152
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,197
all right we have a
desert to get through the

153
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:57,104
time has arrived men
onward toward the northwest

154
00:09:58,380 --> 00:09:59,877
Hey, now, wait just a minute!

155
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:00,790
Hey!

156
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:12,997
Something's wrong.

157
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:13,910
Huh?

158
00:10:13,993 --> 00:10:15,417
I still haven't been able to shake the

159
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:17,997
feeling that someone out
there is watching us.

160
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:18,910
Hmm?

161
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:26,327
Kakyoin, don't you think you
might be worrying a bit too much?

162
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,947
I mean the palm leaves
will erase our tracks.

163
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,937
Plus, we can see for
kilometers in all directions.

164
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:34,902
If someone were here, we'd know.

165
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,474
Actually, I think he's on to something.

166
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,840
I feel some sort of presence, too.

167
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:43,531
Hey, Jotaro, why don't you go take a look?

168
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,357
How about it?

169
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:59,852
Do you see anything suspicious out there?

170
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,577
No, nothing.

171
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:02,778
Nothing whatsoever.

172
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:05,980
Even so, something's not right here.

173
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,242
But what is it?

174
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:11,080
Hey, let's hurry up and go.

175
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,190
Yeah.

176
00:11:13,273 --> 00:11:14,780
Let's get as far away as we can.

177
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,157
We'll keep pressing forward until
the sun goes down this evening,

178
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,960
then stop to pitch our tents.

179
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:23,057
It's much too dangerous
for us to travel at night.

180
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:26,140
I only wish we could get
out of this freaking heat.

181
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:27,439
Just look at this.

182
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:29,462
It's reading 50 degrees Celsius.

183
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,860
Yeah, it is hot out here.

184
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:35,946
But then again, the weather is
at its hottest right around now.

185
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,520
Eight o 'clock? What?

186
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,940
Jotaro, check your watch.

187
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,494
What time does it say?

188
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:45,740
It's ten past eight.

189
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,180
Hey, old man!

190
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,660
My watch is correct.

191
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,660
We lost track of time, but...

192
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:54,611
What the hell's going on?

193
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:57,240
According to my watch, it's past 8 p .m.

194
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:01,060
So why isn't the sun setting?

195
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:03,780
This is impossible.

196
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:07,042
The thermometer is jumping
to 60 degrees Celsius.

197
00:12:14,060 --> 00:12:16,400
No, the sun isn't setting at all.

198
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:17,497
It's actually...

199
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:20,080
It's actually rising higher in the west!

200
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:22,968
Wait, could it be that
that sun is really...

201
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:24,060
A stand?

202
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:36,857
I don't understand how such
a thing is even possible!

203
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:39,234
How could this sun actually be a stand?

204
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,034
Quickly, take cover behind those rocks!

205
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:44,920
How the hell could that sun be a stand?

206
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,880
We're such fools!

207
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,057
How did we miss this?

208
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:50,877
I knew that we were being watched,

209
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:53,737
but I never thought this is
why I couldn't see our stalker.

210
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:56,157
At this rate, that sauna's
gonna burn all day.

211
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,380
No, all night long.

212
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,000
Oh, nom de dieu!

213
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:01,677
It's going to roast us like a
bunch of rotisserie chickens!

214
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,054
We're totally screwed!

215
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:04,810
Yeah.

216
00:13:04,893 --> 00:13:06,518
Though I doubt it'll take that long.

217
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:11,137
The thing is, a sauna can dangerously
raise the body's temperature in minutes.

218
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,985
Okay, then how do we fight it?

219
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:15,315
C 'est des conneries!

220
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,397
It's 70 degrees Celsius!

221
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:21,080
And to add insult to injury, we can't
tell if the stand is close or not.

222
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:23,438
The distance is impossible to judge.

223
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:28,080
Our only option here is to
quickly take out the stand user.

224
00:13:29,180 --> 00:13:30,520
Indeed, the user.

225
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,157
He has to be nearby.

226
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,560
We have to find him.

227
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:36,035
He must have a way to conceal himself.

228
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:38,957
And somehow he's been
following us all this time.

229
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:39,977
Hang on a minute.

230
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:43,097
What if it's like the lovers
we encountered in Pakistan?

231
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:45,697
Maybe this guy has a stand
he can use from far away.

232
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:47,940
Hey, that's not the case this time.

233
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:51,457
Sure, a weak STAN can be
controlled from a distance,

234
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:53,422
but this sun is just too strong.

235
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:56,017
The energy it's emitting is incredible.

236
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:58,240
The STAN user has to be nearby.

237
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,237
Hey, check it out.

238
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,357
The camels are starting to
collapse from exposure to the heat,

239
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:18,020
and this wading isn't getting us anywhere.

240
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:21,537
I'll use Hierophant to do some
reconnaissance around the area.

241
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:25,091
Kakyoin, I'm only searching
for the stand's rough location.

242
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:30,142
Once we know how far away it actually is,
we might just be able to locate the user.

243
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:36,680
20 meters, 40 meters, 60
meters, 80 meters, 100!

244
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:39,814
Something's not right.

245
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:42,180
Kakyoin, have Hierophant come back!

246
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,337
There's something coming right at us!

247
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:46,800
Before that happens, Emeralds!

248
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:50,690
No!

249
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:51,800
